   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "Let \\( f(x) = 2 x^{2} - 12 x + 21 \\) and \\( g(x) = 2 x + 1 \\). Find the exact total area of the shaded regions shown, which lie between the graphs of f and g from \\( x = 0 \\) to \\( x = 6 \\).",
      "command_verb": "find"
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": 30
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "\\( f(x) - g(x) = 2 \\left(x - 5\\right) \\left(x - 2\\right) \\), so the graphs cross at \\( x = 2 \\) and \\( x = 5 \\), both inside the interval. f is above g before the first crossing and after the second, and below g between them.",
         "rule_named": "intersections and order of the curves"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "The pieces are \\( \\int_{0}^{2} \\left(f(x) - g(x)\\right)\\,dx = \\frac{52}{3} \\), \\( \\int_{2}^{5} \\left(g(x) - f(x)\\right)\\,dx = 9 \\) and \\( \\int_{5}^{6} \\left(f(x) - g(x)\\right)\\,dx = \\frac{11}{3} \\).",
         "mathjson": 9,
         "rule_named": "area of each piece, upper minus lower"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "The total area is the sum of the pieces, \\( 30 \\).",
         "mathjson": 30,
         "rule_named": "additivity of area"
      }
   ],
